    "title": "SWG Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)SWG Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)",
    "text": "SWG Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\nSWG Grants - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nConnect & Network\nClinical practice\nEducation & Training\nResearch & Innovation\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nEHA2027 Congress\nEHA2026 Congress\nCongress archive\nScientific meetings\nMembership\nEHA2027 registration\nEHA2027 program\nEHA2027 abstract submission\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\nEHA2027 sustainability\nEHA2026 Congress platform\nEHA2026 sustainability\nEHA2026 Perspectives Congress Report\nEHA2026 gallery\nEHA2025 Perspectives Congress Reports\nEHA2025 gallery\nEHA2024 Chair's wrap-up\nEHA2024 report\nEHA2024 gallery\nEHA2023 report\nEHA2023 gallery\nFull membership\nJunior membership\nTrial membership\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\nEmeritus membership\nJoint EHA and national society membership\nUsing MyEHA\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\nEHA Mentorship Program\nOur guidelines initiative\nGuidelines by areas of disease\nEHA Guidelines app\nEHA Clinical Guidelines Webinar Series\nBedside Hematology – Rapid Reference\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\nEHA Mentorship Program\nEHA Campus\nLearning paths\nTests and tools\nMentoring and career development\nEuropean Hematology Curriculum\nEntrustable Professional Activities\nLighting the Flame Program\nEHA Diagnosis\nEHA Exam\nProgress Test\nCareer comparison tool\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMaster Class\nResearch training programs\nEHA-EMBO Lab Leadership Course\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\nEHA Mentorship Program\nHemaSphere\nSpecialized Working Groups\nGrants\nTopics-in-Focus program\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\nSWG Grants\nHow to apply to join an SWG\nWebinars and online groups\nSWG Preceptorship Program\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nTuesday, May 6, 2025\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMenu\nClose\nConnect & Network\nEHA2027 Congress\nEHA2027 registration\nEHA2027 program\nEHA2027 abstract submission\nEHA2027 travel grants & abstract awards\nEHA2027 sponsorship opportunities\nEHA2027 details and deadlines\nEHA2027 sustainability\nEHA2026 Congress\nEHA2026 Congress platform\nEHA2026 sustainability\nCongress archive\nEHA2026 Perspectives Congress Report\nEHA2026 gallery\nEHA2025 Perspectives Congress Reports\nEHA2025 gallery\nEHA2024 Chair's wrap-up\nEHA2024 report\nEHA2024 gallery\nEHA2023 report\nEHA2023 gallery\nScientific meetings\nMembership\nFull membership\nJunior membership\nTrial membership\nHealthcare-affiliated professional membership\nEmeritus membership\nJoint EHA and national society membership\nUsing MyEHA\nClinical practice\nOur guidelines initiative\nGuidelines by areas of disease\nEHA Guidelines app\nEHA Clinical Guidelines Webinar Series\nBedside Hematology – Rapid Reference\nEducation & Training\nEHA Campus\nLearning paths\nEuropean Hematology Curriculum\nEntrustable Professional Activities\nLighting the Flame Program\nTests and tools\nEHA Diagnosis\nEHA Exam\nProgress Test\nMentoring and career development\nCareer comparison tool\nEHA Mentorship Program\nMaster Class\nResearch training programs\nEHA-EMBO Lab Leadership Course\nResearch & Innovation\nHemaSphere\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\nSWG Grants\nHow to apply to join an SWG\nWebinars and online groups\nSWG Preceptorship Program\nGrants\nEHA Research Grants\nEHA Bilateral Collaborative Grant\nEHA Innovation Grant\nEHA Kick-off Grant\nEHA Research Mobility Grant\nEHA Grants Hall of Fame\nEHA Travel Grants\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\nScope of our grants\nTopics-in-Focus program\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\nCongress\nHemaSphere\nAbout EHA\nSearch\nJoin EHA\nLogin\nHome\nResearch & Innovation\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSWG Grants\nLeft Sidebar\n3 min read · May 1, 2025\nMay 1, 2025\nShare\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nHow to apply to join an SWG\nWebinars and online groups\nSWG Preceptorship Program\nSWG Grants\nThe call for applications is closed. The next call will be open in 2027.\nWinners will be announced by the end of December 2026.\nThese grants are intended to support small, collaborative SWG-led research projects that strengthen scientific exchange, increase member engagement, and build lasting research networks across the EHA community.\nEvery year, we award grants to projects that will:\nHelp us build a collaborative network\nIncrease engagement within SWGs\nWhat an SWG Grant can cover\nSWG Grants can cover costs related to:\nData management\nData analysis\nSample collections and storage\nThey cannot be used to:\nSupport fellowships\nPay individual salaries\nPurchase substantial equipment\nHow many grants will be avarded per this funding cycle?\nUp to 5 SWG grants, each up to 30,000 EUR\nEligibility\nNon-interventional studies, like retrospective studies or prospective data collection, are eligible for support.\nApplications for basic research projects are also eligible. In these cases, we favor those that:\nTake advantage of the collaborative nature of the SWG network\nEncourage the mutual exchange of expertise\nTo increase diversity and support inclusion within our SWG community, we encourage proposals that involve:\nJunior members\nPartners from underrepresented countries\nIn all cases, the principal investigator(s) (PIs) must be EHA members and SWG members at the time of application.\nIndividual applications are not eligible for this call, because each project must foster collaboration and help build a network within the relevant SWG. Please include other SWG members in your project. Non-SWG or non-EHA members will not be counted as collaborators for this grant.\nAll applications should therefore be communicated internally within the relevant SWG before submission. Applicants will be asked to confirm this in the application.\nThe SWG Chair must submit the application, or be copied on the application email. This confirms that the application was presented to the group in advance. Each SWG may submit no more than 3 applications.\nSelection\nWinning grant applications are selected by the SWG Committee.\nIn making its decision, the committee considers:\n• The scientific quality of the project\n• The importance of the topic for further research/subsequent projects\n• The explanation of the budget needs\n• Cooperation and interaction within the SWG or with other SWGs\n• Other sources of support that are already available for this project\n• The overlap with ongoing/already funded projects\n• The inclusion of junior members and/or partners from underrepresented countries\nHow to apply\nTo apply, complete the application form below and send it to [email protected].\nThe SWG Chair must submit the application, or they must be copied in on your application email.\nThe call for SWG-research initiated grants closed on October 4, 2026 at 23:59 CET. The awardees list will be published on the SWG grants webpage.\nPrevious projects\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nShare\nSpecialized Working Groups\nSupport for SWG scientific meetings\nSWG Grants\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2026\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2025\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2024\nSWG Grant-funded projects, 2023\nHow to apply to join an SWG\nWebinars and online groups\nSWG Preceptorship Program\nJoin EHA\nFull membership\nJunior membership\n60-day trial\nGet involved\nCareer development\nScientific meetings\nAbout us\